window.docContents[127].resolve({"/part-5-applications/ch19-hyperfinite-approximation/#ch19-hyperfinite-approximation":{"contents":"Chapter 19 (Ch19_HyperfiniteApproximation.lean, 4,489 lines) demonstrates the Hyperfinite Approximation paradigm: embed an arbitrary infinite structure S into a hyperfinite substructure S^+ \\subseteq {}^*S, apply a finite theorem to S^+ by Transfer, and restrict or take shadow back to S!\n\n1. De Bruijn–Erdős Graph Coloring Theorem: If every finite subgraph of an infinite graph G = (V, E) is k-colorable, let V^+ \\subseteq {}^*V be a hyperfinite vertex set containing {}^*v for every v \\in V. By Transfer of finite k-colorability, the hyperfinite induced subgraph on V^+ has an internal k-coloring c : V^+ \\to {}^*\\{0, \\dots, k-1\\} = \\{0, \\dots, k-1\\}. Restricting x \\mapsto c({}^*x) colors all of G!2. Boolean Algebras & Stone's Representation Theorem: Every finite Boolean algebra is atomic and isomorphic to the power set of its atoms. Embedding any Boolean algebra B into a hyperfinite subalgebra B^+ \\subseteq {}^*B maps each b \\in B to the set of internal atoms of B^+ below {}^*b, immediately yielding Stone's clopen set representation!3. Hyperfinite Hahn–Banach Extension Theorem: Given a sublinear functional p : E \\to \\mathbb{R} and a linear functional f : U \\to \\mathbb{R} dominated by p on a subspace U \\subseteq E, finite-dimensional one-step extension transfers to extend {}^*f across a hyperfinite-dimensional span E^+ \\supseteq E, and taking the standard part F(v) := \\mathrm{sh}\\bigl(\\Phi({}^*v)\\bigr) produces a global p-dominated linear extension on E—along with norm-preserving Banach extensions and separating dual functionals!\n\nsection\nopen Goldblatt.Ch19\n\n#check @stoneHyperfiniteRep_injective\n#check @isClopen_stoneClopenSet\n#check @hahn_banach_extension\n#check @hahn_banach_norm_preserving\n#check @separating_dual_of_ne\nend\n\n\n","context":"Lectures on the Hyperreals — Interactive Lean 4 & Spatial Edition\u0009Part V — Landmark Applications & Reading Guide","header":"5.4. Chapter 19: Hyperfinite Approximation — Coloring, Stone Duality & Hahn–Banach","id":"/part-5-applications/ch19-hyperfinite-approximation/#ch19-hyperfinite-approximation"}});